  "_plan": "Three plates and four stones, in a hall wide enough that nothing can be jammed anywhere it cannot come out of. The fourth stone is spare on purpose: a player who wedges one still has three, and the hand at the cage says out loud that walking out and back in puts them all home. The pillar at 11,10 is the only obstacle in the open floor, and it exists so the middle stone has to be walked around rather than shoved in a straight line. Two Hall hands stand across the neck at 11-12,13, which is one tile wide, so they cannot be sidestepped."
